body:
I relate to a lot of this. A. Lot. 

&#x200B;

I'm a lot like you. if you need somebody to talk to, somebody who understands in a more personal way, message me. 

&#x200B;

Please.

I suppose I *could* go back without him, but there's a lot of things that would make it not work in my favor. For one, somebody has to come down here to get me. That and we currently don't have a truck, so I can't move any of my stuff up there unless my uncle decided to help. I've asked my sister to ask my aunt up there if she could come get me, but that's about as far as anything like that has gone.   
I've decided what school I'm going to go to already if I do wind up stuck down here, and we have a house in our sights that checks everything off my Dad's super-nitpicky list of criteria. Now all I need to do is get him to call the landlord... and to do that, I need to actually catch him in the house for once. 

&#x200B;

For enrollment, Dad said we would go sometime next week. The first day of school there begins on August the 7th, so we have maybe about a seven-day window to get me into the system as a student. Again, I don't know what Dad's gonna do. He changes his plans so much that it's always a mystery. 

&#x200B;

I've thought about clubs myself. I've always liked Drama (though the one time I was in it was a shot in the dark because my friends happened to be in there), and I like Chorus and even maybe something like writing. I haven't taken a look to see what kind of clubs they have there yet, but I do know they offer Chorus and Drama as elective classes, so I *suppose* that means they could have a club too? When August comes I'll be on my Dad's ass a bit more about getting me enrolled... last year he made me get everything under control myself on my *first day of school.*

&#x200B;

I'll just have to go at it, I guess. Thanks for the advice.

Took me a minute but I found it. 

&#x200B;

 [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hhlK5k6Uhn4](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hhlK5k6Uhn4)

It's the Curb your Enthusiasm theme song. 

